    "spph_dur2": "7 Days / 6 Nights",
    "spph_o1": "The Morocco Photography Desert Tour From Fes is a private journey designed for travelers who want to capture Morocco’s imperial cities, blue streets, mountain landscapes, Sahara dunes, kasbahs, valleys, and traditional villages. This tour combines cultural places, scenic roads, desert light, old architecture, and flexible stops for photography along the route from Fes to Marrakech.",
    "spph_o2": "Your journey starts in Fes, one of Morocco’s oldest imperial cities. The old medina, narrow streets, traditional souks, tanneries, historic gates, and artisan workshops offer many opportunities to photograph daily life, architecture, crafts, and cultural details.",
    "spph_o3": "The route continues north to Chefchaouen, the famous blue city in the Rif Mountains. Chefchaouen is known for its blue-painted streets, mountain views, small squares, and peaceful atmosphere, making it one of the most photogenic towns in Morocco.",
    "spph_o4": "After returning south, the tour crosses the Middle Atlas Mountains through Ifrane, cedar forest areas, Midelt, and the Ziz Valley before reaching Merzouga. In the Sahara desert, you will enjoy camel trekking across the dunes of Erg Chebbi, sunset views, sunrise photography, dinner at the desert camp, and an overnight stay under the stars.",
    "spph_o5": "The final part of the journey takes you through Rissani, Todra Gorges, Dades Valley, Rose Valley, Ouarzazate, Ait Ben Haddou, and the High Atlas Mountains before ending in Marrakech. The Morocco Photography Desert Tour From Fes is ideal for travelers who want a scenic Morocco route with enough time for landscapes, portraits, street photography, architecture, and desert images.",
    "spph_d1_t": "Fes Sightseeing Tour With A Local Guide",
    "spph_d1": "Your Morocco Photography Desert Tour From Fes starts with a guided visit of Fes, one of Morocco’s oldest imperial cities. After breakfast, you will meet a local guide and begin exploring the old medina. The visit can include the narrow streets of Fes el-Bali, traditional souks, historic gates, old schools, artisan workshops, and the famous tanneries. This day gives you many chances to photograph architecture, local crafts, medina life, colors, textures, and traditional details. Lunch can be taken inside or near the medina. In the afternoon, you may visit panoramic viewpoints overlooking the old city before returning to your accommodation. Dinner and overnight stay will be in Fes.",
    "spph_d1_n": "Fes",
    "spph_d2_t": "Fes - Rif Mountains - Chefchaouen",
    "spph_d2": "After breakfast, we leave Fes and drive north towards Chefchaouen. The road passes through hills, small towns, and mountain landscapes before reaching the Rif Mountains. Upon arrival in Chefchaouen, you will have free time to explore the old medina. You can walk through the blue-painted streets, visit the main square, enjoy local food, and take photos around the peaceful alleys. Chefchaouen is known for its blue walls, traditional doors, narrow lanes, mountain views, and relaxed rhythm, making it one of the best photography stops in northern Morocco. Dinner and overnight stay will be at a hotel or riad in Chefchaouen.",
    "spph_d2_n": "Chefchaouen",
    "spph_d3_t": "Chefchaouen - Volubilis - Meknes - Fes",
    "spph_d3": "After breakfast, you will have more free time in Chefchaouen for morning photography before we leave the blue city and drive towards Volubilis. Morning light can be a good time to capture the quiet streets and mountain atmosphere. Volubilis is one of Morocco’s most important Roman archaeological sites. You will have time to photograph the ruins, old columns, mosaics, open landscapes, and historic remains. After visiting Volubilis, we continue to Meknes, one of Morocco’s imperial cities. In Meknes, you can visit the old medina area, Bab Mansour, and some historical places linked to the city’s imperial past. After the visit, we return to Fes. Dinner and overnight stay will be at a hotel or riad in Fes.",
    "spph_d3_n": "Fes",
    "spph_d4_t": "Fes - Ifrane - Cedar Forest - Midelt - Ziz Valley - Merzouga Desert",
    "spph_d4": "After breakfast, we leave Fes and travel towards the Sahara desert. The route passes through Ifrane, known for its clean streets and mountain atmosphere. After Ifrane, we continue to the cedar forest near Azrou, where Barbary monkeys can sometimes be seen in their natural surroundings. The journey continues through the Middle Atlas Mountains towards Midelt. After a short break, we drive through the Ziz Valley, famous for its palm groves and panoramic viewpoints. Several stops can be made along the way for photos before continuing towards Erfoud and Merzouga. By the afternoon or evening, we arrive in Merzouga, near the dunes of Erg Chebbi. Dinner and overnight stay will be at a hotel or riad near the desert.",
