    "sphm_d2_n": "Desert camp, Merzouga",
    "sphm_d3_t": "Explore Merzouga Area - Khamlia - Nomad Families - Desert Hotel",
    "sphm_d3": "Wake up early to enjoy the sunrise over the dunes before breakfast at the camp. After breakfast, we return from the camp and begin exploring the Merzouga area. The visit can include Khamlia village, known for its Gnawa music, and nearby desert areas with black volcanic landscapes around the dunes. You may also visit nomad families living around the desert region and learn more about their traditional way of life. The route continues through small desert villages, palm areas, and viewpoints around Erg Chebbi. This day gives you more time to enjoy the Sahara at a slower and more relaxed pace. Dinner and overnight stay will be at a hotel or riad near Merzouga.",
    "sphm_d3_n": "Hotel or riad near Merzouga",
    "sphm_d4_t": "Merzouga Desert - Rissani - Alnif - Draa Valley - Ouarzazate",
    "sphm_d4": "After breakfast, we leave Merzouga and drive towards Rissani, a historic town known for its traditional market and old caravan history. After visiting Rissani, the journey continues through Alnif and the desert landscapes of southern Morocco before reaching the Draa Valley. This long palm valley is known for its old kasbahs, traditional villages, palm groves, and desert atmosphere. We continue through the valley road towards Agdz and then Ouarzazate. Along the way, several stops can be made for photos, coffee, or short breaks. Dinner and overnight stay will be at a hotel or riad in Ouarzazate.",
