    "spjw_dur": "8 Days / 7 Nights",
    "spjw_dur2": "8 Days / 7 Nights",
    "spjw_o1": "The Morocco Jewish Heritage Tour From Casablanca is a cultural journey designed for travelers who want to explore Morocco through its Jewish history, imperial cities, old medinas, mellahs, synagogues, cemeteries, coastal towns, and traditional neighborhoods. This tour combines Casablanca, Rabat, Meknes, Fes, Marrakech, Essaouira, and the Atlantic coast in one balanced itinerary.",
    "spjw_o2": "Your journey starts in Casablanca, Morocco’s largest city and one of the important centers of Jewish heritage in the country. Depending on availability and opening times, the visit can include Jewish heritage places, synagogues, cultural sites, and the Hassan II Mosque from the outside.",
    "spjw_o3": "From Casablanca, the route continues to Rabat and Meknes before reaching Fes, one of Morocco’s oldest imperial cities. In Fes, you will discover the old medina, the Jewish quarter, traditional streets, historic gates, and heritage sites connected to the city’s long cultural history.",
    "spjw_o4": "The journey continues to Marrakech, where you can explore the old medina, the Mellah, traditional souks, and historic monuments with a local guide. After Marrakech, the route continues to Essaouira, a coastal town known for its old medina, Atlantic views, and important Jewish heritage.",
    "spjw_o5": "The Morocco Jewish Heritage Tour From Casablanca is ideal for travelers looking for a meaningful cultural route through Morocco’s imperial cities, Jewish quarters, historic sites, local traditions, and Atlantic coastal heritage.",
    "spjw_d1_t": "Welcome to Casablanca",
    "spjw_d1": "Your Morocco Jewish Heritage Tour From Casablanca starts with pick-up from your accommodation, airport, or port in Casablanca. Depending on your arrival time, we can begin with a short visit of the city. You may visit the Hassan II Mosque from the outside, enjoy the Atlantic coast area, and explore parts of Casablanca connected to the city’s modern history. Depending on availability and opening times, the visit can also include Jewish heritage places in Casablanca. Dinner is optional. Overnight stay will be at a hotel in Casablanca.",
    "spjw_d1_n": "Casablanca",
    "spjw_d2_t": "Casablanca - Rabat - Meknes - Fes",
    "spjw_d2": "After breakfast, we leave Casablanca and drive towards Rabat, the capital city of Morocco. In Rabat, you can visit the Hassan Tower, Mohammed V Mausoleum, the Kasbah of the Udayas, and the old medina area. After visiting Rabat, we continue towards Meknes, one of Morocco’s imperial cities. In Meknes, you can explore the old medina area, Bab Mansour, and historical places linked to the city’s imperial past. The journey continues to Fes. By the evening, we arrive in Fes. Dinner is optional. Overnight stay will be at a hotel or riad in Fes.",
    "spjw_d2_n": "Fes",
    "spjw_d3_t": "Fes Jewish Heritage and Medina Tour",
    "spjw_d3": "After breakfast, you will meet a local guide for a full-day visit of Fes. The visit can include the old medina, traditional souks, historic gates, artisan areas, and important cultural places in the city. You will also explore the Jewish quarter of Fes, known as the Mellah. Depending on access and opening times, the visit can include Jewish heritage sites, old streets, cemetery areas, and buildings connected to the Jewish history of the city. Fes is one of Morocco’s most important cultural cities, and this day gives you time to discover both the old medina and the heritage of the Jewish community that lived there for centuries. Dinner is optional. Overnight stay will be in Fes.",
    "spjw_d3_n": "Fes",
    "spjw_d4_t": "Fes - Ifrane - Beni Mellal - Marrakech",
    "spjw_d4": "After breakfast, we leave Fes and travel towards Marrakech through the Middle Atlas region. The road passes through Ifrane, a mountain town known for its clean streets and calm atmosphere. We continue through mountain landscapes, small towns, and open countryside towards Beni Mellal. Several stops can be made along the way for photos, coffee, or short breaks. After Beni Mellal, the journey continues towards Marrakech. By the afternoon or evening, we arrive in the red city. Dinner is optional. Overnight stay will be at a hotel or riad in Marrakech.",
    "spjw_d4_n": "Marrakech",
    "spjw_d5_t": "Marrakech Jewish Heritage and Medina Tour",
    "spjw_d5": "After breakfast, you will meet a local guide for a full-day visit of Marrakech. The visit can include the old medina, traditional souks, Bahia Palace, Koutoubia Mosque from the outside, and Jemaa el-Fna square. You will also visit the Mellah of Marrakech, the historic Jewish quarter of the city. Depending on access and opening times, the visit can include heritage places, cemetery areas, local streets, and sites connected to the Jewish history of Marrakech. In the afternoon, you may continue exploring the medina, visit local craft areas, or enjoy free time in the city. Dinner is optional. Overnight stay will be in Marrakech.",
    "spjw_d5_n": "Marrakech",
    "spjw_d6_t": "Marrakech - Essaouira",
    "spjw_d6": "After breakfast, we leave Marrakech and drive towards Essaouira on the Atlantic coast. Along the way, you may see argan trees, small villages, and open countryside before reaching the coastal town. Upon arrival in Essaouira, you will have time to explore the old medina, sea walls, fishing port, and blue-and-white streets. Essaouira is known for its relaxed atmosphere, Atlantic views, local crafts, and important Jewish heritage. Depending on availability and opening times, the visit can include the old Mellah area and heritage sites connected to the Jewish community of Essaouira. Dinner is optional. Overnight stay will be at a hotel or riad in Essaouira.",
    "spjw_d6_n": "Essaouira",
    "spjw_d7_t": "Essaouira Jewish Heritage Tour - Free Time",
    "spjw_d7": "After breakfast, you will continue exploring Essaouira with a local guide. The visit can include the old medina, the Mellah area, coastal walls, traditional streets, and heritage places connected to the city’s Jewish history. Essaouira was one of Morocco’s most important Atlantic towns for trade and cultural exchange. Its Jewish heritage can still be seen through old neighborhoods, cemetery areas, and historic buildings. In the afternoon, you will have free time to walk along the coast, enjoy the medina, visit local shops, or relax near the sea. Dinner is optional. Overnight stay will be in Essaouira.",
    "spjw_d7_n": "Essaouira",
    "spjw_d8_t": "Essaouira - Casablanca",
    "spjw_d8": "After breakfast, we leave Essaouira and drive back towards Casablanca along the Atlantic direction. Several stops can be made along the way for coffee, photos, or short breaks. Depending on your departure time, we can go directly to Casablanca airport, port, or your accommodation. If time allows, you may enjoy a final short visit in Casablanca before the tour ends. The Morocco Jewish Heritage Tour From Casablanca ends with drop-off in Casablanca.",
