    "sgo_eyebrow": "Tours from Ouarzazate",
    "sgo_title": "Ouarzazate Desert Tours – The Door to the Sahara",
    "sgo_intro": "Ouarzazate sits where the High Atlas meets the desert, a city of earthen kasbahs and film studios with Ait Ben Haddou just down the road. From here, two great routes lead to the Sahara: east along the Dades and Todra gorges, or south through the palm groves of the Draa Valley. With Morocco Adventures Tour, every trip from Ouarzazate is private, starts at your hotel and is guided by a local team that knows both roads well.",
    "sgo_why_t": "Why start your desert trip in Ouarzazate?",
    "sgo_why_p": "Ouarzazate is already on the desert side of the Atlas. You skip the mountain crossing on day one and reach the gorges, the oases and the dunes sooner, then finish in Marrakech, Fes or back in Ouarzazate.",
    "sgo_inc_t": "What our Ouarzazate tours include",
    "sgo_inc_p": "Each tour page shows exactly what is included. In general, our tours from Ouarzazate come with:",
    "sgo_opt_t": "Our routes from Ouarzazate",
    "sgo_hl_t": "What you will live on the way",
    "sgo_who_t": "Who are these tours for?",
    "sgo_cus_t": "Make the trip your own",
    "sgo_cus_p": "Every itinerary on this page can be adapted. A few ideas travelers often add:",
    "sgo_end_t": "Starting from Ouarzazate?",
    "sgo_end_p": "Send us your dates and the number of travelers. We reply within 24 hours with a clear plan and price, with no obligation.",
    "ozm5_t1": "5 Days Sahara Trip",
    "ozm5_t2": "from Ouarzazate to Marrakech",
    "ozm5_eyebrow": "Ouarzazate · Sahara · Fes · Chefchaouen · Marrakech",
    "ozm5_dur": "5 days",
    "ozm5_dur2": "5 days",
    "ozm5_o1": "Embark on an unforgettable 5-day Sahara trip from Ouarzazate to Marrakech, a journey that takes you through Morocco’s most iconic landscapes. From cinematic kasbahs to the towering dunes of Erg Chebbi, and the winding alleys of Chefchaouen to the vibrant city of Marrakech, this tour blends adventure, history, and culture into one incredible experience.",
    "ozm5_h1": "Explore the ancient Kasbahs of Ouarzazate, the gateway to the desert",
    "ozm5_h2": "Discover the stunning Dades and Todra Gorges, nature’s dramatic masterpieces",
    "ozm5_h3": "Experience the Sahara with a camel trek and a night in a luxury desert camp",
    "ozm5_h4": "Visit the blue-hued town of Chefchaouen, Morocco’s “Blue Pearl”",
    "ozm5_h5": "Stroll through the historic medinas of Fes and Marrakech",
    "ozm5_d1_t": "Ouarzazate to Dades Gorges – Through the Valley of a Thousand Kasbahs",
    "ozm5_d1": "Begin your adventure in Ouarzazate, visiting the famous Kasbah Ait Benhaddou, a UNESCO World Heritage Site, and explore its cinematic landscapes. Travel through the Valley of Roses and the lush Skoura Oasis, reaching the breathtaking Dades Gorges by evening. Overnight stay in a traditional riad in Dades.",
    "ozm5_d1_n": "Traditional riad in the Dades",
    "ozm5_d2_t": "Dades Gorges to Merzouga – Into the Sahara Desert",
    "ozm5_d2": "Head to the dramatic Todra Gorges and walk between their towering cliffs, before journeying to the desert town of Merzouga. In the afternoon, embark on a camel trek across the golden dunes of Erg Chebbi, where you’ll watch the sunset over the Sahara. End your day at a luxury desert camp, experiencing traditional Berber hospitality and enjoying dinner under a blanket of stars.",
    "ozm5_d2_n": "Luxury desert camp",
    "ozm5_d3_t": "Merzouga to Fes – Journey Through History",
    "ozm5_d3": "After a magical sunrise in the desert, begin your journey north to Fes. Pass through the Ziz Valley, dotted with palm groves, and stop at the cedar forests of the Middle Atlas Mountains, home to Barbary monkeys. Arrive in Fes by evening and explore its bustling medina.",
    "ozm5_d3_n": "Fes",
    "ozm5_d4_t": "Fes to Chefchaouen – The Blue Pearl of Morocco",
    "ozm5_d4": "Depart Fes in the morning and head to Chefchaouen, a picturesque town nestled in the Rif Mountains. Wander through its charming blue-washed streets, visit the main square and the Kasbah Museum, soak in its relaxed vibe, and enjoy the local cuisine. Overnight stay in a cozy riad.",
    "ozm5_d4_n": "Cozy riad in Chefchaouen",
    "ozm5_d5_t": "Chefchaouen to Marrakech – End Your Adventure in the Red City",
    "ozm5_d5": "Conclude your journey with a drive to Marrakech, Morocco’s vibrant cultural hub, through the scenic landscapes of northern Morocco, with stops at notable landmarks along the way. In Marrakech, explore its bustling souks, the vibrant Jemaa el-Fnaa square and the historic medina. The tour ends with drop-off at your accommodation.",
