    "sgf_title": "Fes Desert Tours – From the Imperial City to the Sahara",
    "sgf_intro": "Few journeys in Morocco show as many contrasts as the road from Fes to the Sahara. You leave the maze of the oldest medina in the country, climb into the cedar forests of the Middle Atlas, follow the palm groves of the Ziz Valley and arrive at the golden dunes of Erg Chebbi. With Morocco Adventures Tour, each desert trip from Fes is private, built around your dates and guided by a local team that drives this road every week.",
    "sgf_why_t": "Why start your desert trip in Fes?",
    "sgf_why_p": "Fes is the closest imperial city to Merzouga, and the drive itself is part of the trip: mountains, forests, oases and finally the sand. You can return to Fes or continue south and west to Marrakech.",
