    "er3_t1": "3 Days Errachidia",
    "er3_t2": "to Merzouga Desert Tour",
    "er3_eyebrow": "Errachidia · Merzouga · Marrakech or Fes",
    "er3_dur": "3 days",
    "er3_dur2": "3 days",
    "er3_o1": "Are you ready for a true desert adventure? This 3-day desert tour from Errachidia to Merzouga, and ending in Marrakech or Fes, is the perfect way to explore Morocco’s stunning desert landscapes, fascinating culture, and iconic sites. From camel treks in the Erg Chebbi dunes to vibrant desert towns and unique cultural experiences, this tour offers the ultimate Moroccan desert experience.",
    "er3_h1": "Journey through the stunning Ziz Valley and Todra Gorge",
    "er3_h2": "Experience an unforgettable camel trek in the Sahara Desert",
    "er3_h3": "Spend the night at a luxury desert camp under the stars",
    "er3_h4": "Visit historical Kasbahs, desert oases, and charming towns",
    "er3_h5": "End your tour in the vibrant cities of Marrakech or Fes",
    "er3_d1_t": "Errachidia to Merzouga – A Scenic Desert Journey",
    "er3_d1": "Your adventure begins in Errachidia, where you will be picked up by your guide and driver. You’ll embark on a scenic drive, passing through the Ziz Valley, which is known for its lush date palm groves and dramatic mountain scenery. Along the way, you’ll stop at Erfoud and Rissani, before continuing your journey towards Merzouga, the gateway to the Sahara Desert. Upon reaching Merzouga, you’ll be greeted by the vast Erg Chebbi dunes and mount your camels for a trek through the golden sands. As you ride through the dunes, you’ll witness the breathtaking beauty of the desert at sunset. Your journey will end at a luxury desert camp, where you’ll enjoy a traditional Berber dinner and sleep under a blanket of stars.",
    "er3_d1_n": "Luxury desert camp",
    "er3_d2_t": "Merzouga to Dades Valley – Todra Gorge, Desert Towns and Kasbahs",
    "er3_d2": "After a spectacular Sahara sunrise, you’ll head back to Merzouga by camel or 4×4, depending on your preference. From there, you’ll begin your drive towards the Dades Valley, one of the most scenic regions in Morocco. Along the way, you’ll stop to explore the historical Kasbahs and Ksar villages that dot the landscape. Along the way, you’ll stop at the majestic Todra Gorge, where you can take a short hike through its towering limestone cliffs. In the afternoon, you’ll arrive in Dades Valley, known for its dramatic gorges and fertile landscapes. The day will end with a peaceful overnight stay in a local hotel or guesthouse, where you can unwind and enjoy a delicious Moroccan dinner.",
    "er3_d2_n": "Local hotel or guesthouse in the Dades Valley",
    "er3_d3_t": "Dades Valley to Marrakech or Fes – Exploring Morocco’s Imperial Cities",
    "er3_d3": "On the final day of your journey, you’ll depart from Dades Valley and head towards either Marrakech or Fes, depending on your preference. The road to Marrakech or Fes is a long one, but you’ll be treated to stunning landscapes, including the High Atlas Mountains, the Ziz River, and the vibrant Berber villages. By evening, you’ll arrive at either Marrakech or Fes, concluding your unforgettable desert adventure.",
