    "tg12_t1": "12 Days Absolute Morocco Tour",
    "tg12_t2": "from Tangier",
    "tg12_eyebrow": "Absolute Morocco from Tangier",
    "tg12_dur": "12 days",
    "tg12_dur2": "12 days",
    "tg12_o1": "Embark on an unforgettable journey across Morocco with this 12-day absolute tour from Tangier, an experience that promises an extraordinary blend of history, culture, and breathtaking landscapes. From the winding blue streets of Chefchaouen to the golden dunes of the Sahara Desert and the bustling medinas of Fes and Marrakech, this itinerary offers a comprehensive exploration of Morocco’s most iconic destinations.",
    "tg12_h1": "Explore the vibrant cities of Tangier, Chefchaouen, Fes, Marrakech, and Casablanca",
    "tg12_h2": "Immerse yourself in the culture and history of ancient sites, including Volubilis, Ait Benhaddou, and imperial cities",
    "tg12_h3": "Experience the magic of the Sahara Desert with a camel trek and luxury desert camp stay",
    "tg12_h4": "Discover breathtaking landscapes, from the Rif and Atlas Mountains to the Dades Valley and Todra Gorge",
    "tg12_d1_t": "Arrival in Tangier – Welcome to Tangier",
    "tg12_d1": "Begin your Moroccan adventure in the vibrant coastal city of Tangier, where the Atlantic Ocean meets the Mediterranean Sea. After your arrival, enjoy a guided tour of the Kasbah Museum, to delve into Tangier’s rich history, the Hercules Caves, to marvel at the fascinating rock formations and ocean views, and Cape Spartel, a stunning viewpoint where the two seas converge. Overnight in a traditional riad in Tangier.",
    "tg12_d1_n": "Traditional riad in Tangier",
    "tg12_d2_t": "Tangier to Chefchaouen – The Blue Pearl of Morocco",
    "tg12_d2": "Travel to Chefchaouen, a picturesque town in the Rif Mountains known for its vibrant blue-painted streets and relaxed atmosphere. Wander through the charming medina, visit the Plaza Uta el-Hammam and the historic Kasbah, and enjoy panoramic views from the hilltop Spanish Mosque. Spend the night in a riad, soaking in the serenity of Chefchaouen.",
    "tg12_d2_n": "Riad in Chefchaouen",
    "tg12_d3_t": "Chefchaouen to Fes via Volubilis and Meknes",
    "tg12_d3": "On the way to Fes, visit Volubilis, Morocco’s best-preserved Roman ruins, adorned with intricate mosaics, and Meknes, a historic imperial city featuring the impressive Bab Mansour Gate and Sahrij Swani Basin. Arrive in Fes for dinner and overnight in a traditional riad.",
    "tg12_d3_n": "Traditional riad in Fes",
    "tg12_d4_t": "Guided Tour of Fes – The Spiritual Capital",
    "tg12_d4": "Spend the day exploring the cultural and spiritual heart of Morocco: Fes el Bali, a UNESCO-listed medina filled with labyrinthine streets, the Al-Qarawiyyin University, the world’s oldest functioning university, the Chouara Tannery, to witness traditional leather-making techniques, and the Bou Inania Madrasa, a stunning example of Moroccan craftsmanship. Enjoy a traditional dinner and spend the night in Fes.",
    "tg12_d4_n": "Fes",
    "tg12_d5_t": "Fes to Merzouga via Ifrane and Midelt – From the Mountains to the Desert",
    "tg12_d5": "Travel through the Middle Atlas Mountains, passing by Ifrane, often called “Morocco’s Switzerland” for its European-style charm, and Azrou, home to ancient cedar forests and Barbary monkeys. Arrive in Merzouga, where you’ll begin your camel trek into the desert. Enjoy dinner and an enchanting night in a luxury Sahara camp under the starry sky.",
    "tg12_d5_n": "Luxury Sahara camp",
    "tg12_d6_t": "Merzouga and the Sahara Desert – Immersive Desert Experience",
    "tg12_d6": "Spend the day exploring the wonders of the Sahara Desert. Witness a mesmerizing sunrise over the dunes, visit a local nomad family to learn about their unique way of life, and explore Khamlia Village, famous for its Gnawa music. Enjoy another magical night in the desert, surrounded by the tranquility of the Erg Chebbi dunes.",
    "tg12_d6_n": "Desert camp in Erg Chebbi",
    "tg12_d7_t": "Merzouga to Dades Valley via Todra Gorge – Dramatic Landscapes",
    "tg12_d7": "After breakfast, travel to the spectacular Todra Gorge, a dramatic canyon with towering cliffs that attract climbers and nature lovers alike. Continue through the Dades Valley, also known as the “Valley of a Thousand Kasbahs,” to see its unique rock formations. Spend the night in a charming hotel overlooking the valley.",
    "tg12_d7_n": "Hotel overlooking the Dades Valley",
    "tg12_d8_t": "Dades Valley to Ouarzazate via Ait Benhaddou – Film Studios and Ancient Fortresses",
    "tg12_d8": "Journey to Ouarzazate, the “Hollywood of Morocco,” home to the Atlas Film Studios, where many Hollywood blockbusters were filmed, and Ait Benhaddou, a UNESCO World Heritage Site and iconic ksar (fortified village). Spend the evening exploring the rich history of Ouarzazate before an overnight stay.",
    "tg12_d8_n": "Ouarzazate",
    "tg12_d9_t": "Ouarzazate to Marrakech via the High Atlas Mountains",
    "tg12_d9": "Cross the majestic High Atlas Mountains via the Tizi n’Tichka Pass, enjoying scenic views and stopping at Berber villages along the way. Arrive in Marrakech, where the vibrant medina awaits. Overnight in a riad in the heart of the city.",
    "tg12_d9_n": "Riad in the heart of Marrakech",
    "tg12_d10_t": "Guided Tour of Marrakech – Exploring the Red City",
    "tg12_d10": "Spend the day uncovering Marrakech’s rich history and vibrant culture: the Koutoubia Mosque, the largest mosque in Marrakech, the Bahia Palace, a masterpiece of Moroccan architecture, the Majorelle Garden, a serene botanical garden created by Jacques Majorelle, and Jemaa el-Fnaa Square, a lively hub of street performers, food stalls, and artisans. Enjoy a farewell dinner in a traditional Moroccan restaurant.",
    "tg12_d10_n": "Riad in Marrakech",
    "tg12_d11_t": "Marrakech to Casablanca – Journey to Casablanca",
    "tg12_d11": "Travel to Casablanca, Morocco’s largest city. Explore its modern and historical attractions, including the Hassan II Mosque, one of the largest mosques in the world, and the Corniche Boulevard, a scenic promenade along the Atlantic Ocean. Spend the night in Casablanca.",
    "tg12_d11_n": "Casablanca",
    "tg12_d12_t": "Departure from Casablanca – Farewell Morocco",
    "tg12_d12": "After breakfast, transfer to the airport for your departure. Reflect on the unforgettable memories and diverse experiences of your 12-day Morocco tour.",
