    "tg10_t1": "10 Days Holiday in Morocco",
    "tg10_t2": "from Tangier",
    "tg10_eyebrow": "Holiday from Tangier",
    "tg10_dur": "10 days",
    "tg10_dur2": "10 days",
    "tg10_o1": "Embark on an unforgettable 10-day holiday in Morocco from Tangier, where you’ll discover the beauty of this diverse and culturally rich country. From the stunning landscapes of the Rif Mountains to the golden dunes of the Sahara Desert, and from historic cities to vibrant markets, this journey offers a perfect blend of adventure, relaxation, and cultural immersion.",
    "tg10_h1": "Explore the historical treasures of Tangier, Chefchaouen, Fes, and Marrakech",
    "tg10_h2": "Witness the stunning landscapes of the Middle Atlas Mountains, Todra Gorge, and the Sahara Desert",
    "tg10_h3": "Experience a camel trek and overnight stay in a luxury Sahara Desert camp",
    "tg10_h4": "Visit UNESCO World Heritage Sites, including Volubilis and Ait Benhaddou",
    "tg10_d1_t": "Arrival in Tangier – Welcome to Morocco",
    "tg10_d1": "Your adventure begins in the vibrant port city of Tangier, where Mediterranean and Atlantic cultures meet. Upon arrival, your guide will greet you and take you to explore the city’s highlights, including the Kasbah Museum, to dive into Tangier’s rich history and artifacts, Cape Spartel, a scenic spot where the two seas meet, and the Hercules Caves, a natural wonder steeped in mythology. Enjoy dinner and spend your first night in a traditional riad.",
    "tg10_d1_n": "Traditional riad in Tangier",
    "tg10_d2_t": "Tangier to Chefchaouen – Journey to the Blue Pearl",
    "tg10_d2": "After breakfast, travel to Chefchaouen, the famous “Blue Pearl” nestled in the Rif Mountains. The drive is scenic, with breathtaking views of rolling hills and picturesque villages. Wander through the city’s winding blue-painted streets, visit Plaza Uta el-Hammam, the vibrant heart of the medina, and explore the historic Kasbah, enjoying panoramic views from its tower. Spend the night in a cozy riad, surrounded by the tranquil ambiance of this unique city.",
    "tg10_d2_n": "Cozy riad in Chefchaouen",
    "tg10_d3_t": "Chefchaouen to Fes – Roman Ruins at Volubilis",
    "tg10_d3": "On your way to Fes, stop at Volubilis, a UNESCO World Heritage Site showcasing the best-preserved Roman ruins in North Africa. Marvel at the ancient mosaics, grand arches, and sprawling layout. Continue to Fes, Morocco’s spiritual and cultural capital. Check into your riad in the medina, where you’ll enjoy a delicious Moroccan dinner.",
    "tg10_d3_n": "Riad in the Fes medina",
    "tg10_d4_t": "Guided Tour of Fes – Discover the Treasures of Fes",
    "tg10_d4": "Spend the day exploring Fes el Bali, the oldest part of the city and a UNESCO-listed site. Highlights include the Al-Qarawiyyin University, the oldest university in the world, the Bou Inania Madrasa, a masterpiece of Islamic architecture, the Chouara Tannery, to witness traditional leather-making methods, and the Royal Palace, known for its impressive golden gates. Enjoy a traditional Moroccan dinner and overnight stay at your riad.",
    "tg10_d4_n": "Riad in Fes",
    "tg10_d5_t": "Fes to Merzouga via Ifrane and Midelt – From Mountains to Desert",
    "tg10_d5": "Begin your journey to the Sahara Desert, traveling through the scenic Middle Atlas Mountains. Stop in Ifrane, known as “Little Switzerland” for its alpine-style architecture, and Azrou, famous for its cedar forests and Barbary monkeys. Arrive in Merzouga, where you’ll trade your vehicle for camels and embark on a trek across the dunes of Erg Chebbi. Enjoy dinner and an unforgettable night under the stars at a luxury desert camp.",
    "tg10_d5_n": "Luxury desert camp in Merzouga",
    "tg10_d6_t": "Merzouga to Dades Valley via Todra Gorge",
    "tg10_d6": "Wake up early to witness a spectacular desert sunrise before returning to Merzouga by camel. Continue your journey to the stunning Todra Gorge, where towering cliffs create a dramatic natural canyon. Travel through the Road of a Thousand Kasbahs to reach the Dades Valley, known for its unique rock formations and traditional Berber villages. Spend the night in a charming kasbah-style hotel.",
    "tg10_d6_n": "Kasbah-style hotel in the Dades Valley",
    "tg10_d7_t": "Dades Valley to Ouarzazate via Ait Benhaddou – Hollywood of Morocco",
    "tg10_d7": "Stop in Ouarzazate, a city famous for its film studios and historical kasbahs. Visit the Taourirt Kasbah before heading to Ait Benhaddou, a UNESCO World Heritage Site and iconic fortified village that has appeared in films like Gladiator and The Mummy. Enjoy dinner and an overnight stay in Ouarzazate.",
    "tg10_d7_n": "Ouarzazate",
    "tg10_d8_t": "Ouarzazate to Marrakech via the High Atlas Mountains",
    "tg10_d8": "Travel along the Tizi n’Tichka Pass, a breathtaking route through the High Atlas Mountains, dotted with Berber villages. Stop at scenic viewpoints and learn about traditional life in the region. Arrive in Marrakech, where the bustling Jemaa el-Fnaa Square and vibrant souks await. Check into your riad and enjoy an evening of exploration.",
    "tg10_d8_n": "Riad in Marrakech",
    "tg10_d9_t": "Guided Tour of Marrakech – Exploring the Red City",
    "tg10_d9": "Discover Marrakech’s historical and cultural treasures, including the Koutoubia Mosque, the largest mosque in Marrakech, with an iconic minaret, the Bahia Palace, a stunning example of Moroccan craftsmanship, the Majorelle Garden, a tranquil oasis designed by French artist Jacques Majorelle, and the Medina and Souks, to wander through vibrant markets filled with spices, textiles, and handcrafted goods. Spend your final evening enjoying a farewell dinner.",
    "tg10_d9_n": "Riad in Marrakech",
    "tg10_d10_t": "Departure – End of Your Moroccan Adventure",
    "tg10_d10": "After breakfast, transfer to the airport in Marrakech or return to Tangier, depending on your travel plans. Reflect on the unforgettable memories of your 10-day holiday in Morocco.",
