    "tg7_t1": "7 Days Tour",
    "tg7_t2": "from Tangier to Marrakech",
    "tg7_eyebrow": "Tangier to Marrakech",
    "tg7_dur": "7 days",
    "tg7_dur2": "7 days",
    "tg7_o1": "Embark on an exciting 7-day journey from Tangier to Marrakech, uncovering Morocco’s rich culture, history, and breathtaking landscapes. From the serene blue streets of Chefchaouen to the lively souks of Marrakech, this week-long tour will take you through the highlights of Morocco, including Fes, the Sahara Desert, and the majestic Atlas Mountains.",
    "tg7_h1": "Wander through the enchanting blue medina of Chefchaouen",
    "tg7_h2": "Explore the historic alleys of Fes Medina, a UNESCO World Heritage Site",
    "tg7_h3": "Experience the magic of the Sahara, with a camel trek and a night in a luxury desert camp",
    "tg7_h4": "Marvel at the beauty of the Middle Atlas Mountains, valleys, and gorges",
    "tg7_h5": "Discover the cinematic charm of Ait Ben Haddou, a famous ksar",
    "tg7_h6": "Immerse yourself in the vibrant culture of Marrakech, the “Red City”",
    "tg7_d1_t": "Tangier to Chefchaouen – The Blue Pearl",
    "tg7_d1": "Your adventure begins in Tangier, where you’ll travel to the picturesque town of Chefchaouen, nestled in the Rif Mountains. Famous for its striking blue-painted streets, Chefchaouen is a photographer’s dream and a serene escape. Wander through its narrow blue alleys, visit the central Plaza Uta el-Hammam and relax at a local café, and enjoy the scenic views from Ras El Ma spring.",
    "tg7_d1_n": "Chefchaouen",
    "tg7_d2_t": "Chefchaouen to Fes – Journey Through History",
    "tg7_d2": "Leave the blue city behind and travel to Fes, stopping at fascinating historical landmarks along the way. Discover Volubilis, Morocco’s best-preserved Roman ruins, explore the imperial city of Meknes, including Bab Mansour and the royal stables, then arrive in Fes, where you’ll begin exploring the world-famous medina.",
    "tg7_d2_n": "Fes",
    "tg7_d3_t": "Fes – Explore the Cultural Capital",
    "tg7_d3": "Spend the day exploring the rich history and culture of Fes, Morocco’s oldest imperial city and a UNESCO World Heritage Site. Visit the Al-Qarawiyyin University, the oldest existing university in the world, see the colorful Chouara Tanneries, where leather is dyed traditionally, and wander through the vibrant souks to admire the stunning Bou Inania Madrasa.",
    "tg7_d3_n": "Fes",
    "tg7_d4_t": "Fes to Merzouga – Into the Desert",
    "tg7_d4": "Leave Fes early and embark on a scenic drive to Merzouga, the gateway to the Sahara Desert, through the breathtaking landscapes of the Middle Atlas Mountains. Stop in the charming alpine-style town of Ifrane, spot Barbary macaques in their natural habitat in the Azrou cedar forest, and marvel at the lush palm groves of the Ziz Valley. Arrive in Merzouga and enjoy a camel trek through the golden dunes of Erg Chebbi, followed by a night under the stars in a luxury desert camp.",
    "tg7_d4_n": "Luxury desert camp in Merzouga",
    "tg7_d5_t": "Merzouga to Dades Valley – Landscapes and Gorges",
    "tg7_d5": "Wake up early to catch the sunrise over the dunes before continuing your journey to the Dades Valley, passing through stunning desert and mountain landscapes. Visit the dramatic Todra Gorge, a popular spot for hiking and rock climbing, then discover the picturesque Dades Valley, known for its kasbahs and rock formations called the “Monkey Fingers.”",
    "tg7_d5_n": "Dades Valley",
    "tg7_d6_t": "Dades Valley to Marrakech – The Road of a Thousand Kasbahs",
    "tg7_d6": "Travel to Marrakech through the scenic High Atlas Mountains, making stops at iconic landmarks along the way. Explore the historic Ait Ben Haddou, a UNESCO World Heritage Site and a famous filming location, drive through the stunning Tizi n’Tichka pass, one of Morocco’s highest mountain roads, and arrive in Marrakech, where the energy and charm of the city await.",
    "tg7_d6_n": "Marrakech",
    "tg7_d7_t": "Explore Marrakech – The Red City",
    "tg7_d7": "Spend your final day discovering the vibrant city of Marrakech, filled with rich history, colorful souks, and exquisite architecture. Visit the iconic Jemaa el-Fnaa Square, alive with storytellers, musicians, and food vendors, admire the stunning Koutoubia Mosque and its minaret, and stroll through the tranquil Majorelle Garden, a lush oasis in the heart of the city. Your unforgettable 7-day journey concludes in Marrakech, leaving you with lasting memories of Morocco.",
