    "tg5_t1": "5 Days Tour",
    "tg5_t2": "from Tangier to Marrakech",
    "tg5_eyebrow": "Tangier to Marrakech",
    "tg5_dur": "5 days",
    "tg5_dur2": "5 days",
    "tg5_o1": "Embark on a 5-day journey from Tangier to Marrakech, exploring Morocco’s rich culture, historic cities, and breathtaking landscapes. This itinerary combines scenic drives, camel trekking, and a night in a luxury desert camp, making it a perfect introduction to Morocco’s magic.",
    "tg5_h1": "Wander the charming streets of Chefchaouen, the Blue City",
    "tg5_h2": "Discover the cultural heritage of Fes, Morocco’s oldest imperial city",
    "tg5_h3": "Experience the magic of the Sahara with a camel ride and a stay in a luxury camp",
    "tg5_h4": "Travel through the scenic Middle Atlas Mountains and the stunning Dades Valley",
    "tg5_h5": "End your adventure in vibrant Marrakech, known for its bustling souks and iconic landmarks",
    "tg5_d1_t": "Tangier to Chefchaouen – The Blue Pearl",
    "tg5_d1": "Begin your journey in Tangier, a city where Europe and Africa meet, and head south to the picturesque town of Chefchaouen, nestled in the Rif Mountains. Explore the charming blue-painted streets of the medina and enjoy its peaceful atmosphere, relax in Plaza Uta el-Hammam with a cup of Moroccan mint tea, and visit the serene Ras El Ma spring with its panoramic mountain views.",
    "tg5_d1_n": "Chefchaouen",
    "tg5_d2_t": "Chefchaouen to Fes – A Journey Through History",
    "tg5_d2": "Depart Chefchaouen and make your way to Fes, stopping en route at the ancient Roman ruins of Volubilis and the imperial city of Meknes. Marvel at the well-preserved Roman mosaics and structures of Volubilis, visit the impressive Bab Mansour gate and the royal granaries in Meknes, then arrive in Fes, home to the world’s largest car-free urban area and a UNESCO World Heritage Site.",
    "tg5_d2_n": "Fes",
    "tg5_d3_t": "Fes to Merzouga – Gateway to the Sahara",
    "tg5_d3": "Leave Fes early for a scenic drive to the Sahara Desert, passing through the lush Middle Atlas Mountains and quaint Berber villages. Stop in Ifrane, the charming town known as “Little Switzerland”, spot Barbary macaques in the Azrou cedar forest and admire the sweeping views of palm groves and desert landscapes in the Ziz Valley. Upon arrival in Merzouga, embark on a camel trek into the golden dunes of Erg Chebbi, where you’ll spend the night in a luxury desert camp.",
    "tg5_d3_n": "Luxury desert camp in Merzouga",
    "tg5_d4_t": "Merzouga to Dades Valley – Journey Through the Heart of Morocco",
    "tg5_d4": "Wake up early to witness a breathtaking Sahara sunrise before heading towards the scenic Dades Valley. Take a stroll through the Todra Gorge, a dramatic canyon with towering cliffs, then discover the Dades Valley, the “Valley of a Thousand Kasbahs”, and enjoy its stunning landscapes of red rock formations and lush oases.",
    "tg5_d4_n": "Dades Valley",
    "tg5_d5_t": "Dades Valley to Marrakech – Crossing the High Atlas",
    "tg5_d5": "Conclude your journey with a drive to Marrakech, crossing the spectacular High Atlas Mountains. Explore Ait Ben Haddou, a UNESCO World Heritage Site and famous ksar that has served as the backdrop for many films, enjoy breathtaking views as you wind through the Tizi n’Tichka pass, and reach the Red City in the late afternoon, where you can explore its lively souks and iconic landmarks.",
    "tg5_d5_n": "Marrakech",
    "tg5_x1": "Plane ticket",
