    "fs7_t1": "7 Days Morocco Tour",
    "fs7_t2": "from Fes",
    "fs7_eyebrow": "Private tour · imperial cities & the Sahara",
    "fs7_dur": "7 days · 6 nights",
    "fs7_dur2": "7 days",
    "fs7_o1": "A complete first journey through Morocco in one week: the medieval medina of Fes, the cedar forests of the Middle Atlas, a night in the Sahara, the gorges and kasbahs of the south, a full day in Marrakech and a last stop in Casablanca before your flight.",
    "fs7_o2": "You start with two nights in Fes and a guided day in Fes el-Bali, among its tanneries, madrasas and craft souks. Then the road crosses Ifrane and the Ziz Valley to Merzouga, where a camel takes you into the dunes of Erg Chebbi for a night in a desert camp.",
    "fs7_o3": "After the Todra Gorge and a night in the Dades Valley, you visit Ait Ben Haddou and cross the High Atlas to Marrakech, where a full day is yours to discover its squares, palaces and gardens. The trip ends in Casablanca, by the Hassan II Mosque, before your transfer to the airport.",
    "fs7_h1": "Guided day in the Fes medina",
    "fs7_h2": "Ifrane & the Azrou cedar forest",
    "fs7_h3": "Camel trek & Erg Chebbi camp",
    "fs7_h4": "Todra Gorge & Dades Valley",
    "fs7_h5": "Ait Ben Haddou & Tizi n’Tichka",
    "fs7_h6": "Marrakech & the Hassan II Mosque",
    "fs7_d1_t": "Arrival in Fes",
    "fs7_d1": "We welcome you on arrival and drive you to your riad in or near the medina. The rest of the day is free to rest or take a first walk through the lanes of the old city, one of the great UNESCO World Heritage medinas.",
    "fs7_d1_n": "Riad in Fes",
    "fs7_d2_t": "Guided day in Fes",
    "fs7_d2": "With a local guide, explore Fes el-Bali: the Al-Qarawiyyin mosque and university, often called the oldest still in activity, the Chouara tannery seen from a leather-shop terrace, and the carved cedar and zellige of the 14th-century Bou Inania madrasa. Meet craftsmen in the souks and taste local street food along the way.",
    "fs7_d2_n": "Riad in Fes",
    "fs7_d3_t": "Fes – Ifrane – Ziz Valley – Merzouga",
    "fs7_d3": "Drive into the Middle Atlas, stopping in Ifrane, the alpine-style town known as the Switzerland of Morocco, and in the cedar forest of Azrou to meet the Barbary macaques. Continue south through Midelt and along the palm groves of the Ziz Valley. In Merzouga, ride a camel into the Erg Chebbi dunes at sunset to your camp for dinner under the stars.",
    "fs7_d3_n": "Desert camp in Erg Chebbi",
    "fs7_d4_t": "Merzouga – Todra Gorge – Dades",
    "fs7_d4": "Wake early for sunrise over the dunes, have breakfast at camp and return to Merzouga by camel or 4×4. Drive west to the Todra Gorge and walk along the river between its high cliffs, then continue to the Dades Valley, the valley of a thousand kasbahs, for dinner and the night.",
    "fs7_d4_n": "Riad or guesthouse in the Dades Valley",
    "fs7_d5_t": "Dades – Ait Ben Haddou – Marrakech",
    "fs7_d5": "Follow the road of the kasbahs past Ouarzazate to Ait Ben Haddou, the UNESCO-listed earthen ksar, and walk its lanes up to the top for the view. Then cross the High Atlas over the Tizi n’Tichka pass, among peaks, terraced fields and Berber villages, and arrive in Marrakech in the evening.",
    "fs7_d5_n": "Riad in Marrakech",
    "fs7_d6_t": "A full day in Marrakech",
    "fs7_d6": "Discover the Red City: the Koutoubia minaret, the painted rooms and courtyards of the Bahia Palace, the cobalt-blue Majorelle Garden and the souks of the medina. In the evening, enjoy dinner in a traditional restaurant and the lights and music of Jemaa el-Fnaa.",
    "fs7_d6_n": "Riad in Marrakech",
    "fs7_d7_t": "Marrakech – Casablanca",
    "fs7_d7": "Drive north to Casablanca, about three hours away. Depending on your flight time, visit the Hassan II Mosque, built over the Atlantic, and take a walk along the Corniche before your transfer to Mohammed V airport.",
    "fs7_i1": "Airport welcome in Fes and transfer to Casablanca airport",
    "fs7_i2": "Private air-conditioned vehicle, fuel included",
    "fs7_i3": "Professional English-speaking driver-guide",
    "fs7_i4": "Local guides for the Fes medina and Marrakech",
