    "fm5_t1": "5 Days Desert Tour",
    "fm5_t2": "from Fes to Marrakech",
    "fm5_eyebrow": "Private tour · the relaxed way from Fes to Marrakech",
    "fm5_dur": "5 days · 4 nights",
    "fm5_dur2": "5 days",
    "fm5_o1": "The most comfortable way to travel from Fes to Marrakech through the Sahara. With a first night in Midelt, the long drive south is split in two, so you arrive in the dunes rested and every day keeps time for walks, stops and photos.",
    "fm5_o2": "From the cedar forests of the Middle Atlas you follow the Ziz Valley and the fossil town of Erfoud to Merzouga, where a camel carries you into the dunes of Erg Chebbi for a night in a desert camp. Then come Rissani, the Todra Gorge and a night in the Dades Valley.",
    "fm5_o3": "The last two days follow the road of the kasbahs: the Skoura oasis, Ouarzazate, and Ait Ben Haddou on the way to the Tizi n’Tichka pass and Marrakech.",
    "fm5_h1": "Ifrane & the Azrou cedar forest",
    "fm5_h2": "Ziz Valley & Erfoud fossils",
    "fm5_h3": "Camel trek & Erg Chebbi camp",
    "fm5_h4": "Todra Gorge & Dades Valley",
    "fm5_h5": "Skoura oasis & Kasbah Amridil",
    "fm5_h6": "Ait Ben Haddou & Tizi n’Tichka",
    "fm5_d1_t": "Fes – Ifrane – Azrou – Midelt",
    "fm5_d1": "Leave Fes in the morning and drive into the Middle Atlas. Walk the tidy streets of Ifrane, the alpine-style town known as the Switzerland of Morocco, then meet the Barbary macaques in the cedar forest of Azrou. Continue to Midelt, the apple town set between the Middle and High Atlas, for lunch, a relaxed afternoon and the night.",
    "fm5_d1_n": "Hotel or guesthouse in Midelt",
    "fm5_d2_t": "Midelt – Ziz Valley – Erfoud – Merzouga",
    "fm5_d2": "Cross the Tizi n’Talghemt pass and descend into the Ziz Valley, a long ribbon of date palms and earthen villages, with stops at the viewpoints. In Erfoud, visit a fossil workshop to see the marine fossils polished from the local stone. In Merzouga, ride a camel into the Erg Chebbi dunes at sunset to your camp for dinner and Berber music under the stars.",
    "fm5_d2_n": "Desert camp in Erg Chebbi",
    "fm5_d3_t": "Merzouga – Rissani – Todra Gorge – Dades",
    "fm5_d3": "Wake early for sunrise over the dunes, have breakfast and return to Merzouga by camel or 4×4. Stroll through the souks of Rissani, with their spices, fabrics and crafts, then walk between the 300-metre cliffs of the Todra Gorge. Continue to the Dades Valley, with its kasbahs and rock formations, for dinner and the night.",
    "fm5_d3_n": "Riad or guesthouse in the Dades Valley",
    "fm5_d4_t": "Dades – Skoura – Ouarzazate",
    "fm5_d4": "Drive along the road of the kasbahs to the Skoura palm oasis and visit Kasbah Amridil, one of the best-preserved in Morocco. In Ouarzazate, the desert’s film capital, visit the Taourirt kasbah or the Atlas Film Studios before dinner and the night in a riad.",
    "fm5_d4_n": "Riad or hotel in Ouarzazate",
    "fm5_d5_t": "Ouarzazate – Ait Ben Haddou – Marrakech",
    "fm5_d5": "Start the day at Ait Ben Haddou, the UNESCO ksar seen in Gladiator and The Mummy, and walk its winding lanes in the soft morning light. Then cross the High Atlas over the Tizi n’Tichka pass, among peaks, terraced fields and Berber villages. Arrival at your riad or hotel in Marrakech in the afternoon.",
    "fm5_i1": "Pick-up from your riad or hotel in Fes",
