    "fm4_t1": "4 Days Desert Tour",
    "fm4_t2": "from Fes to Marrakech",
    "fm4_eyebrow": "Private tour · Fes to Marrakech at an easy pace",
    "fm4_dur": "4 days · 3 nights",
    "fm4_dur2": "4 days",
    "fm4_o1": "Four days to travel from Fes to Marrakech the long and beautiful way, with time to enjoy each stage: the cedar forests of the Middle Atlas, a night in the Sahara, the gorges and kasbah valleys of the south, and the crossing of the High Atlas.",
    "fm4_o2": "After Ifrane, Azrou and the Ziz Valley, a camel takes you into the dunes of Erg Chebbi for a night in a desert camp. The next day you visit Rissani, walk in the Todra Gorge and sleep in the Dades Valley.",
    "fm4_o3": "The third day is the day of the kasbahs: the Skoura oasis and Kasbah Amridil, Ouarzazate and the UNESCO ksar of Ait Ben Haddou, where you spend the night, before crossing the Tizi n’Tichka to Marrakech.",
    "fm4_h1": "Ifrane & the Azrou cedar forest",
    "fm4_h2": "Camel trek & Erg Chebbi camp",
    "fm4_h3": "Rissani market & medfouna",
    "fm4_h4": "Todra Gorge & Dades Valley",
    "fm4_h5": "Skoura oasis & Kasbah Amridil",
    "fm4_h6": "A night at Ait Ben Haddou",
    "fm4_d1_t": "Fes – Ifrane – Midelt – Merzouga",
    "fm4_d1": "Leave Fes in the morning and climb into the Middle Atlas. Stop in Ifrane, the alpine-style town known as the Switzerland of Morocco, then meet the Barbary macaques in the cedar forest of Azrou. Lunch in Midelt, between the Middle and High Atlas, then follow the palm groves of the Ziz Valley south. In Merzouga, ride a camel into the Erg Chebbi dunes at sunset to your camp for dinner and Berber music under the stars.",
    "fm4_d1_n": "Desert camp in Erg Chebbi",
    "fm4_d2_t": "Merzouga – Rissani – Todra Gorge – Dades",
    "fm4_d2": "Wake early for sunrise over the dunes, have breakfast and return to Merzouga by camel or 4×4. Visit Rissani and its old souks, where you can taste medfouna, the stuffed Berber bread of the region. Walk between the 300-metre cliffs of the Todra Gorge, then continue to the Dades Valley, with its kasbahs and the rock formations known as the Monkey Fingers.",
    "fm4_d2_n": "Riad or guesthouse in the Dades Valley",
    "fm4_d3_t": "Dades – Skoura – Ouarzazate – Ait Ben Haddou",
    "fm4_d3": "Drive through the Skoura palm oasis and visit Kasbah Amridil, one of the best-preserved kasbahs in Morocco. Continue to Ouarzazate to see the Taourirt kasbah, then reach Ait Ben Haddou, the UNESCO ksar seen in Gladiator and Game of Thrones. Walk its narrow lanes up to the granary at the top for the view, and spend the night nearby.",
    "fm4_d3_n": "Kasbah hotel at Ait Ben Haddou",
    "fm4_d4_t": "Ait Ben Haddou – Tizi n’Tichka – Marrakech",
    "fm4_d4": "Cross the High Atlas over the Tizi n’Tichka pass, with its winding road, rugged peaks and Berber villages, stopping for photos along the way. Arrival at your riad or hotel in Marrakech in the early afternoon.",
    "fm4_i1": "Pick-up from your riad or hotel in Fes",
