    "fm3_t1": "3 Days Desert Tour",
    "fm3_t2": "from Fes to Marrakech",
    "fm3_eyebrow": "Private tour · Fes to Marrakech via the Sahara",
    "fm3_dur": "3 days · 2 nights",
    "fm3_dur2": "3 days",
    "fm3_o1": "The most rewarding way to travel between Fes and Marrakech: instead of the motorway, you cross the Middle Atlas, sleep in the Sahara and return over the High Atlas, seeing the great landscapes of Morocco in three full days.",
    "fm3_o2": "The first day takes you through Ifrane, the cedar forests of Azrou and the Ziz Valley to Merzouga, where a camel carries you into the Erg Chebbi dunes at sunset. After a night in a desert camp, you visit Rissani, walk in the Todra Gorge and reach the Dades Valley.",
    "fm3_o3": "The last day follows the road of the kasbahs to Ouarzazate and Ait Ben Haddou, then climbs over the Tizi n’Tichka pass and down into Marrakech by late afternoon.",
    "fm3_h1": "Ifrane & Azrou cedar forest",
    "fm3_h2": "Ziz Valley palm oasis",
    "fm3_h3": "Camel trek & Erg Chebbi camp",
    "fm3_h4": "Sunrise over the dunes",
