    "fm3_h6": "Ait Ben Haddou & Tizi n’Tichka",
    "fm3_d1_t": "Fes – Ifrane – Midelt – Merzouga",
    "fm3_d1": "Leave Fes early and climb into the Middle Atlas. Stop in Ifrane, the tidy alpine-style town often called the Switzerland of Morocco, then meet the Barbary macaques in the cedar forest near Azrou. Lunch in Midelt, then descend through the Ziz Valley and its palm groves. In Merzouga, ride a camel into the Erg Chebbi dunes at sunset to your camp, for dinner, Berber music by the fire and a night under the stars.",
    "fm3_d1_n": "Desert camp in Erg Chebbi",
    "fm3_d2_t": "Merzouga – Rissani – Todra Gorge – Dades",
    "fm3_d2": "Wake early for sunrise over the dunes, have breakfast and return to Merzouga by camel or 4×4. Visit Rissani, an old caravan town with a lively market, then walk along the river in the Todra Gorge between its high cliffs. Continue to the Dades Valley, known for its kasbahs and strange rock formations, for the night.",
    "fm3_d2_n": "Riad or guesthouse in the Dades Valley",
    "fm3_d3_t": "Dades – Ouarzazate – Ait Ben Haddou – Marrakech",
    "fm3_d3": "Follow the road of the kasbahs to Ouarzazate and see the Taourirt kasbah. Visit Ait Ben Haddou, the UNESCO-listed earthen ksar seen in Gladiator and Game of Thrones, then cross the High Atlas over the Tizi n’Tichka pass, one of the highest roads in the country. Arrival in Marrakech in the late afternoon.",
    "fm3_i1": "Pick-up from your riad or hotel in Fes",
