    "mk7_t1": "7 Days Sahara Desert Tour",
    "mk7_t2": "from Marrakech",
    "mk7_eyebrow": "Private tour · two nights in the Sahara",
    "mk7_dur": "7 days · 6 nights",
    "mk7_dur2": "7 days",
    "mk7_o1": "A full week to travel from Marrakech into the Sahara at an easy pace: mountain passes, earthen kasbahs, deep gorges, palm valleys and, at the heart of the trip, two nights among the golden dunes of Erg Chebbi.",
    "mk7_o2": "After a first afternoon in the medina of Marrakech, you cross the High Atlas to Ait Ben Haddou and the Dades Valley, walk in the Todra Gorge and ride a camel into the dunes at sunset. A second desert day leaves time for sunrise, a nomad family and the Gnawa music of Khamlia.",
    "mk7_o3": "The way back follows a different road: the Saghro mountains and Alnif, Zagora on the old caravan route, the long palm groves of the Draa Valley and Ouarzazate, before a last crossing of the Atlas and a farewell dinner in Marrakech.",
    "mk7_h1": "Marrakech medina & Jemaa el-Fnaa",
    "mk7_h2": "Tizi n’Tichka & Ait Ben Haddou",
    "mk7_h3": "Dades Valley & Todra Gorge",
    "mk7_h4": "Two nights in the Erg Chebbi dunes",
    "mk7_h5": "Nomads & Gnawa music in Khamlia",
    "mk7_h6": "Zagora & the Draa palm groves",
    "mk7_d1_t": "Arrival in Marrakech",
    "mk7_d1": "We welcome you in Marrakech and take you to your riad. In the afternoon, walk through the medina and its souks of spices, leather and lanterns, and end the day in Jemaa el-Fnaa as the square fills with musicians, storytellers and food stalls.",
    "mk7_d1_n": "Riad in Marrakech",
    "mk7_d2_t": "Marrakech – Ait Ben Haddou – Dades Valley",
    "mk7_d2": "Cross the High Atlas over the Tizi n’Tichka pass, with wide views over peaks and Berber villages. Visit the UNESCO ksar of Ait Ben Haddou, a backdrop for many films, then pass through Ouarzazate and continue to the Dades Valley and its red rock formations.",
    "mk7_d2_n": "Riad in the Dades Valley",
    "mk7_d3_t": "Dades – Todra Gorge – Merzouga",
    "mk7_d3": "Walk along the river at the bottom of the Todra Gorge, between cliffs around 300 metres high. Continue across the desert plains to Merzouga, then ride a camel into the Erg Chebbi dunes at sunset to reach your camp for dinner under the stars.",
    "mk7_d3_n": "Desert camp in Erg Chebbi",
    "mk7_d4_t": "A full day in the Sahara",
    "mk7_d4": "Wake early for sunrise over the dunes. During the day, meet a nomad family to learn about life in the desert and visit Khamlia, a village known for its Gnawa music. Back at camp, enjoy a relaxed evening, dinner and a sky full of stars.",
    "mk7_d4_n": "Desert camp in Erg Chebbi",
    "mk7_d5_t": "Merzouga – Alnif – Zagora",
    "mk7_d5": "Leave the dunes and drive along the Saghro mountains to Alnif, a small town known for its fossils, with a lunch stop on the way. Arrive in Zagora, the old gateway to the caravan routes, and see the famous sign announcing 52 days to Timbuktu.",
    "mk7_d5_n": "Guesthouse in Zagora",
    "mk7_d6_t": "Zagora – Draa Valley – Ouarzazate",
    "mk7_d6": "Drive up the Draa Valley, one of the largest palm groves in Morocco, lined with Berber villages and old kasbahs. In Ouarzazate, visit the Taourirt kasbah or the Atlas Film Studios before dinner and a quiet night in a riad.",
    "mk7_d6_n": "Riad in Ouarzazate",
    "mk7_d7_t": "Ouarzazate – Marrakech",
    "mk7_d7": "Cross the High Atlas one last time, with photo stops along the way. Back in Marrakech, close your journey with a farewell dinner in a traditional Moroccan restaurant.",
    "mk7_i1": "Welcome and transfers in Marrakech",
