    "mf4_t1": "4 Days from Marrakech",
    "mf4_t2": "to Fes via the Desert",
    "mf4_eyebrow": "Private desert tour · one way",
    "mf4_dur": "4 days · 3 nights",
    "mf4_dur2": "4 days",
    "mf4_o1": "The relaxed way from Marrakech to Fes: four days across the High Atlas, into the Sahara and up through the Middle Atlas, with one more night on the road so every stage is easy and every stop has time.",
    "mf4_o2": "You visit Ait Ben Haddou and Ouarzazate, sleep in the Dades Valley, walk in the Todra Gorge and ride a camel into the Erg Chebbi dunes for a night in a desert camp.",
    "mf4_o3": "The road north follows the palm groves of the Ziz Valley to Midelt, then crosses the cedar forests of Azrou — home of the Barbary macaques — and Ifrane, the “Switzerland of Morocco”, before Fes.",
    "mf4_h1": "Ait Ben Haddou & Ouarzazate",
    "mf4_h2": "Dades Valley & Todra Gorge",
    "mf4_h3": "Camel trek & desert camp",
    "mf4_h4": "Ziz Valley palm groves",
    "mf4_h5": "Azrou cedars & macaques",
    "mf4_h6": "Ifrane, the Switzerland of Morocco",
    "mf4_d1_t": "Marrakech – Ait Ben Haddou – Dades Valley",
    "mf4_d1": "Leave Marrakech in the morning and cross the High Atlas over the Tizi n’Tichka pass at 2,260 m. Explore the UNESCO ksar of Ait Ben Haddou and climb to the top for the view, then visit Ouarzazate and its Taourirt kasbah, and the Atlas film studios if time allows. Through the Rose Valley you reach the Dades Valley for a Moroccan dinner and the night.",
    "mf4_d1_n": "Hotel or riad in Dades Valley",
    "mf4_d2_t": "Dades – Todra Gorge – Merzouga",
    "mf4_d2": "Walk along the river in the Todra Gorge, where red cliffs rise over 300 metres. Continue through Berber villages and palm groves to Erfoud, known for its fossil workshops, and on to Merzouga. In the late afternoon, ride a camel into the Erg Chebbi dunes at sunset to reach your camp for dinner, Berber music and a night under the stars.",
    "mf4_d2_n": "Desert camp in Merzouga",
    "mf4_d3_t": "Merzouga – Ziz Valley – Midelt",
    "mf4_d3": "Sunrise over the dunes, breakfast at the camp and back to Merzouga by camel or 4×4. Drive north along the palm groves of the Ziz Valley, with stops at its viewpoints, to Midelt, the town of apple orchards at the foot of the mountains. Night in a guesthouse with a warm dinner.",
    "mf4_d3_n": "Guesthouse in Midelt",
    "mf4_d4_t": "Midelt – Azrou – Ifrane – Fes",
    "mf4_d4": "Cross the Middle Atlas to Azrou and walk in its cedar forest, where you may meet the Barbary macaques. Stop in Ifrane, the alpine-style town known as the Switzerland of Morocco, then arrive in Fes in the late afternoon, where we drop you at your accommodation.",
    "mf4_i1": "Pick-up in Marrakech and drop-off at your accommodation in Fes",
    "mf4_i2": "Private air-conditioned vehicle, fuel included",
    "mf4_i3": "Professional English-speaking driver-guide",
    "mf4_i4": "1 night in Dades Valley and 1 night in Midelt",
    "mf4_i5": "1 night in a desert camp in Erg Chebbi",
    "mf4_i6": "Camel trek into the dunes",
    "mf4_i7": "3 breakfasts and 3 dinners",
