    "mf3_t1": "3 Days from Marrakech",
    "mf3_t2": "to Fes via the Desert",
    "mf3_eyebrow": "Private desert tour · one way",
    "mf3_dur": "3 days · 2 nights",
    "mf3_dur2": "3 days",
    "mf3_o1": "The best way to travel between Marrakech and Fes is through the Sahara. In three days you cross the High Atlas, follow the valleys of the south, sleep in the dunes of Erg Chebbi and climb north through palm groves and cedar forests to the oldest imperial city of Morocco.",
    "mf3_o2": "Day one takes you over the Tizi n’Tichka pass to the UNESCO ksar of Ait Ben Haddou, seen in Gladiator and Game of Thrones, then through Ouarzazate and the Rose Valley to the Dades Valley, the “valley of a thousand kasbahs”.",
    "mf3_o3": "On day two you walk in the Todra Gorge and ride a camel into the dunes of Merzouga for sunset and a night in a desert camp. On day three, after sunrise over the sand, the road leads through the Ziz Valley, Midelt and the cedar forests of Azrou to Fes.",
    "mf3_h1": "Tizi n’Tichka & Ait Ben Haddou",
    "mf3_h2": "Rose Valley & Dades",
    "mf3_h3": "Todra Gorge",
    "mf3_h4": "Camel trek & desert camp",
    "mf3_h5": "Ziz Valley palm groves",
    "mf3_h6": "Azrou cedars & macaques",
    "mf3_d1_t": "Marrakech – Ait Ben Haddou – Dades Valley",
    "mf3_d1": "An early start from Marrakech into the High Atlas over the Tizi n’Tichka, one of the highest road passes in Morocco, with views of terraced fields and Berber villages. Explore the alleys of Ait Ben Haddou and climb to the top, then stop in Ouarzazate for lunch and the Taourirt kasbah. Through the Rose Valley you reach the Dades Valley at sunset for a Moroccan dinner and the night.",
    "mf3_d1_n": "Hotel or riad in Dades Valley",
    "mf3_d2_t": "Dades – Todra Gorge – Merzouga",
    "mf3_d2": "Walk along the river in the Todra Gorge, between walls up to 300 metres high. Cross the Tafilalet region through Tinjdad and Erfoud — a good stop to taste medfouna, the Berber stuffed bread. In Merzouga, camels take you into the Erg Chebbi dunes for sunset, followed by dinner, music around the fire and a night in a comfortable desert camp.",
    "mf3_d2_n": "Desert camp in Merzouga",
    "mf3_d3_t": "Merzouga – Ziz Valley – Midelt – Fes",
    "mf3_d3": "Sunrise over the dunes and breakfast at the camp, then back to Merzouga by camel or 4×4. Drive north through the palm groves of the Ziz Valley to Midelt, the “apple capital” of Morocco, for lunch. Cross the Middle Atlas and stop in the cedar forest of Azrou to see the Barbary macaques, then descend to Fes, where we drop you at your accommodation.",
    "mf3_i1": "Pick-up in Marrakech and drop-off at your accommodation in Fes",
    "mf3_i2": "Private air-conditioned vehicle, fuel included",
    "mf3_i3": "Professional English-speaking driver-guide",
    "mf3_i4": "1 night in a hotel or riad in Dades Valley",
    "mf3_i5": "1 night in a desert camp in Erg Chebbi",
    "mf3_i6": "Camel trek into the dunes",
    "mf3_i7": "2 breakfasts and 2 dinners",
